{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness","id":925504,"title":"Liberation through Corruption - or, bringing Setites to the Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-03T14:53:04-07:00","id":925504,"title":"Liberation through Corruption - or, bringing Setites to the Chronicles of Darkness","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tl;dr:</b> I'd like to get your opinions on some of the roadblocks I have encountered during my latest pet project - translating the essence of the Setite Clan from VtM fame to the Chronicles of Darkness setting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, I know what you are thinking: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Boo, Hiss! Why bring old Clans into the new setting? Just go play VtM!</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> But please hear me out!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>So what is it I am trying to do?</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would like to create a covenant and/or bloodline that captures the core theme about the Setites from VtM: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberation through corruption</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They believe themselves to be holy warriors in the fight against the Aeons - Godlike beings who have trapped humanity in the physical world through a construct of arbitrary laws and rules. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The only way to free humanity from this cage is to enlighten them about the true nature of the world and to reveal their inner strength to them. The only way to facilitate this liberation? Absolute and complete corruption followed by complete rejection of the fake material world and consequently, transcendence. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, I am having problems to decide on the approach I should take here as either option seems to have a number of pros and cons.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Covenant</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pros:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Ability to include Kindred from all different Clans.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- At its core this belief set seems to be about shared politics and ethics instead of shared </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">blood, making it a potentially better fit for a covenant,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cons:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unclear on how to implement them rule wise? A covenant wide shared discipline? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Easier interaction with mortals?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Overall the result here would be similar to the Circle. Basically, these guys could be a local offshot of which worships mythical serpents associated with destruction or corruption like Set, Typhon, the </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Serpent in Eden (sometimes associated with Lucifer as promethean analogy). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tl;dr: I'd like to get your opinions on some of the roadblocks I have encountered during my latest pet project - translating the essence of the Setite Clan from VtM fame to the Chronicles of Darkness setting.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, I know what you are thinking: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Boo, Hiss! Why bring old Clans into the new setting? Just go play VtM!</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> But please hear me out!</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So what is it I am trying to do?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would like to create a covenant and/or bloodline that captures the core theme about the Setites from VtM: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberation through corruption</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They believe themselves to be holy warriors in the fight against the Aeons - Godlike beings who have trapped humanity in the physical world through a construct of arbitrary laws and rules. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The only way to free humanity from this cage is to enlighten them about the true nature of the world and to reveal their inner strength to them. The only way to facilitate this liberation? Absolute and complete corruption followed by complete rejection of the fake material world and consequently, transcendence. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, I am having problems to decide on the approach I should take here as either option seems to have a number of pros and cons.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Covenant</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pros:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Ability to include Kindred from all different Clans.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- At its core this belief set seems to be about shared politics and ethics instead of shared </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">blood, making it a potentially better fit for a covenant,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cons:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unclear on how to implement them rule wise? A covenant wide shared discipline? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Easier interaction with mortals?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Overall the result here would be similar to the Circle. Basically, these guys could be a local offshot of which worships mythical serpents associated with destruction or corruption like Set, Typhon, the </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Serpent in Eden (sometimes associated with Lucifer as promethean analogy). \\</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pros: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Specific abilities could be implemented as a bloodline discipline + devotions.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cons: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unsure about which parent clan this might fit best with. The Daeva (helpfully nicknamed </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Serpents) and their theme of seduction seem like a good fit, however I also see something of the Mekhet in them</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unsure about what a good bloodline weakness would be.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Bloodline approach would severely limit these guy\u2019s recruitment capabilities. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pros: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Specific abilities could be implemented as a bloodline discipline + devotions.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cons: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unsure about which parent clan this might fit best with. The Daeva (helpfully nicknamed </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Serpents) and their theme of seduction seem like a good fit, however I also see something of the Mekhet in them</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unsure about what a good bloodline weakness would be.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Bloodline approach would severely limit these guy\u2019s recruitment capabilities. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, what do you think? Any and all advice is welcome! </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feeling inspired? Feel free to drop some powers/rituals/(nick)-names you think might be appropriate for these guys.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","user":"Lepaca","date":". 07-03-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:04:33-07:00","id":925517,"title":"","content":"You might check out the Mercy Seat of Belial's Brood. They have a twist on that belief whereupon they will be granted return to the Adversary when Heaven is empty, and thus work to corrupt every soul to ensure they stay mired in the world of the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> For serpent powers you might check out the Gorgons from the Circle of the Crone book, they have their own Discipline, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Amphivena\" target=\"_blank\">Amphivena</a>, revolving around serpents.<br /> <br /> If you want a straight Setite-to-Requiem conversion you could grab it from the Vampire Translation Guide, which also has a conversion for Serpentis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-03-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:35:39-07:00","id":925532,"title":"","content":"Have you had a look at the Followers if Seth in Clanbook: Mekhet? Their niche is &quot;liberation through chaos&quot;, so they're not quite the same thing, but they share a lot of DNA with the WoD Setites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:53:04-07:00","id":925538,"title":"","content":"Optional Cocktail<ul><li>The Society of the Accord p.117 The Danse Macabre -Base-</li> <li>Mystery Cult Initiation p.121 Blood and Smoke -Twist the Accords ideology, while remaining apart of the Covenant-</li> <li>Sidebar: Two Clans, One Bloodline p.162 Ordo Dracul -Daeva/Mekhet- Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor and...</li> </ul>-Edit-<br /> I understand that they had Presence in VtM, but I would forgo giving them Majesty this go around in favor of Auspex. To this end the allure of these Kindred would be less rooted in supernatural awe and more in manipulating desires you didn't even have to vocalize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","user":"Panopticon","date":". 07-03-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","name":"Panopticon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:13:46-07:00","id":925655,"title":"","content":"How is this different from merely being a Set-focused CotC cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:15:20-07:00","id":926177,"title":"","content":"Warning: Long reply incoming. Thanks for all your insights so far!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=925517#post925517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might check out the Mercy Seat of Belial's Brood. They have a twist on that belief whereupon they will be granted return to the Adversary when Heaven is empty, and thus work to corrupt every soul to ensure they stay mired in the world of the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> For serpent powers you might check out the Gorgons from the Circle of the Crone book, they have their own Discipline, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Amphivena\" target=\"_blank\">Amphivena</a>, revolving around serpents.<br /> <br /> If you want a straight Setite-to-Requiem conversion you could grab it from the Vampire Translation Guide, which also has a conversion for Serpentis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the tip! The Mercy Seat were an interesting read, especially given that, while they act in a similar fashion they appear to be doing it for more or less completely opposite reasons. Definately, something to consider.<br /> <br /> Amphivena would be a great inspiration source if I decide to go the BL route (and also to keep the serpent theme as a core tennet), thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=925532#post925532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you had a look at the Followers if Seth in Clanbook: Mekhet? Their niche is &quot;liberation through chaos&quot;, so they're not quite the same thing, but they share a lot of DNA with the WoD Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I don't have Clanbook: Mekhet yet, but I will be sure to check them out. Also, a pretty obvious miss from my side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Panopticon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=925538#post925538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Optional Cocktail<ul><li>The Society of the Accord p.117 The Danse Macabre -Base-</li> <li>Mystery Cult Initiation p.121 Blood and Smoke -Twist the Accords ideology, while remaining apart of the Covenant-</li> <li>Sidebar: Two Clans, One Bloodline p.162 Ordo Dracul -Daeva/Mekhet- Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor and...</li> </ul>-Edit-<br /> I understand that they had Presence in VtM, but I would forgo giving them Majesty this go around in favor of Auspex. To this end the allure of these Kindred would be less rooted in supernatural awe and more in manipulating desires you didn't even have to vocalize.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great comments all around. Love the Society of the Accord and merging them with MCI is a great idea. <br /> Also, If I end up going for the BL option a kind of merged bloodline between these two seems to be like a good call. I do however think that Majesty would fit the concept quite well, so I might aim for Auspex, Obfuscate, Majesty + X (serpent-ish maybe)? What worries me about that discipline spread though is that is fairly far removed from either parent Clan option.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=925655#post925655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this different from merely being a Set-focused CotC cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. In my imagination this group would be less focused on serving a particular deity (while maybe still using it as a metaphor for their framework) and more about self-empowerment. Also, potentially no blood magic and Set/other mystical serpents don't really fit the Dark Mother/Crone archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:36:59-07:00","id":926310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=926177#post926177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question. In my imagination this group would be less focused on serving a particular deity (while maybe still using it as a metaphor for their framework) and more about self-empowerment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not uncommon for Acolyte coteries/city structures to stick with one flavor of paganism over others, and the Circle is all about self-empowerment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, potentially no blood magic and Set/other mystical serpents don't really fit the Dark Mother/Crone archetype. </div> </div> </div>Lack of blood magic would definitely be a difference. Other than that:<br /> <br /> 1. Set is not a serpent deity. In addition to their progenitor, Set, the oWoD Setites also worshiped Apep, a serpent demon from the Egyptian mythology. This is how they got their serpentine themes and powers, Set himself had nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> 2. The Circle is much more eclectic in its range of beliefs than you give them credit for. And they literally have a serpent's head prominently displayed in their logo! Of course serpent deities are in theme for them!<br /> <br /> One thing I don't think anybody mentioned so far is that the Khaibit bloodline, at least in their 1e writeup, was originally a militant cult of Set venerating his role as protector of Egypt's threshold and demon hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:40:23-07:00","id":926503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness?p=926177#post926177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I don't have Clanbook: Mekhet yet, but I will be sure to check them out. Also, a pretty obvious miss from my side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's well worth a read, and you get a lot of bang for your buck; Shadows in the Dark is easily my favourite of the five Requiem Clanbooks. Some of the systems are a little out of date now, but it only requires a little elbow grease to bring them into Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:53:01-07:00","id":927835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925504-liberation-through-corruption-or-bringing-setites-to-the-chronicles-of-darkness#post925504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cons: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Unsure about which parent clan this might fit best with.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sister Bloodlines of Mekhet and Daeva with several Devotions that use Majesty and Auspex, have the bloodlines weaknesses be mirror images of the two clans (Mekhet Setites get the Daeva's weakness and Daeva Setites get the Mekhet weakness.)<br /> <br /> Sensing temptation weak points and the ability to seduce others into temptation fit so beautifully together it'd be a shame to separate them. Darkness and Seduction belong together in the Setite bloodlines.<br /> <br /> However I think the Mekhet would be the Progenitor clan folding in the Daeva later, as the Egyptian versus Hindi name origins seem to suggest.<br /> <br /> Also an advantage of the bloodlines is using Apep and Set flavored cults within the Circle of the Crone so you don't have to rework blood sorcery from scratch and can have some Cruac Setite Devotions, possibly one that reduces vampires from the three other clans back down to revenants so they can be uplifted into becoming Mekhet or Daeva Setites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-07-2016, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T18:31:31-07:00","id":930636,"title":"","content":"Definitely sounds like a Circle cult. If you want serpent based abilities instead of Cruac, then make it an initiation rite that they have to swear off Cruac in order to join the cult and gain the serpentine powers or make the serpent power <i>be</i> Cruac but they are forbidden from learning rituals outside of the select few you wish them to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:58:34-07:00","id":930915,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest perhaps this bloodline being a minor Mage crossover? When I ST, I kinda use VtM rather than VtR, but I've found how the Setites and the Seers of the Throne could make quite perfect enemies. The Exarchs sound close enough to the Aeons, and in my own mind it makes for a perfect evil vs evil campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T08:59:41-07:00","id":932533,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late reply.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> : Wow, thanks for the tipp about Shadows in the Dark. Really good read and well worth it!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar582_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"582\" data-vbnamecard=\"582\">Morangias</a>: You are absolutely right. After giving it some thought I think that the Circle cult approach might actually work.<br /> <br /> Also thanks for reminding me about the Apep distinction! If I remember correctly Set actually defeated (devoured?) Apep which gave his childer the serpent-themed powers. This in turn means that I have a pretty good reason for not including any serpentine stuff in my cult if I don't want to. Neat! (@Rathamus: Thanks for the idea, but I would actually prefer to stick with 'normal' Cruac if I can get away without the serpent imagery).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a>: Sister bloodlines as the core of the cult seem like a great idea!<br /> <br /> @SaullotetheGentle: Thanks for the tipp. I know next to nothing about Mage but I read the wiki article about the Seers and they really seem like a match made in heaven! I will however need to make sure that the scope of the campaign doesn't become to cosmis if I choose to include them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for all the replies, really helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T09:40:32-07:00","id":933453,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly there was an Elder Setite power that basically made their form like an avatar of Setekh, size increase and Set Animal head. That sounds like a Vigor + Protean Devotion to me that is likely cult specific. Previous editions of vampire have seriously muddled the Apep and Setekh relationship. Personally I think it would be awesome if they were opposing cults, with Apep being Balal's brood for their covenant and Setites being Crone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I think you should make the Apepites a gangel bloodline as the carnage and snake transformation powers would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-18-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}